EXPERIMENT 7: Transfer Learning for Image Classification
Algorithm
1. Import the required libraries.
2. Load the CIFAR-10 image dataset.
3. Preprocess and resize the images.
4. Load a pre-trained MobileNetV2 model without its top layer.
5. Freeze the pre-trained layers.
6. Add new classification layers.
7. Compile and train the model.
8. Evaluate the model on test data.
9. Display the test accuracy.
Code

import tensorflow as tf
from tensorflow.keras import layers, models

# Load CIFAR-10 dataset
(x_train, y_train), (x_test, y_test) = tf.keras.datasets.cifar10.load_data()

# Use a small portion for simple training
x_train = tf.image.resize(x_train[:10000], (96, 96))
x_test = tf.image.resize(x_test[:2000], (96, 96))

y_train = y_train[:10000]
y_test = y_test[:2000]

# Load pre-trained MobileNetV2
base_model = tf.keras.applications.MobileNetV2(
    weights='imagenet',
    include_top=False,
    input_shape=(96, 96, 3)
)

# Freeze pre-trained layers
base_model.trainable = False

# Create model
model = models.Sequential([
    base_model,
    layers.GlobalAveragePooling2D(),
    layers.Dense(10, activation='softmax')
])

# Compile
model.compile(
    optimizer='adam',
    loss='sparse_categorical_crossentropy',
    metrics=['accuracy']
)

# Train
model.fit(x_train, y_train, epochs=2, batch_size=32)

# Evaluate
loss, accuracy = model.evaluate(x_test, y_test)

print("Test Accuracy:", accuracy)

